+### Per-frame signature hash for guarantors
+
+Guarantors need to commit to a tx shape that includes the data of *another* VERIFY frame (the sender's). `compute_sig_hash` elides every VERIFY frame's data, so a guarantor signing it cannot bind the sender VERIFY data. `compute_frame_sig_hash(tx, frame_index)` resolves this by eliding only the frame currently executing and preserving every other VERIFY frame's data, so the guarantor's signature covers the sender's VERIFY data without self-referencing the guarantor's own signature bytes.
