+### Guarantor Risk and Griefing
+
+A guarantor backing a tx whose sender VERIFY fails absorbs the gas. The canonical paymaster's guarantor-mode signature binds `TXPARAM(0x0B)`, which covers the sender VERIFY frame's data; this prevents an attacker from mutating the sender VERIFY data after the guarantor signs. Without this, a guarantor signing only the canonical tx hash could be griefed by an attacker swapping in a sender signature that always fails.
+
+Guarantor commitments must be paired with a `bumpNonce` frame structurally enforced by the canonical paymaster runtime, so that the paymaster's per-sender guarantor nonce advances even when sender VERIFY fails. Without this, a guarantor signature would be replayable.
+
+### Per-signer Stream State
+
+Each non-zero `(sender, signer)` stream consumes one storage slot in `AUTH_MANAGER` (SSTORE-from-zero, 20 000 gas). State growth is bounded economically and by `MAX_ACTIVE_SIGNERS_PER_SENDER` in the public mempool. Pruning / reclamation is out of scope for v1; senders migrate to a new `signer` value before reaching `MAX_NONCE - 1` on the current one.
+
+### Signer Binding Scope
+
+The verified-signers table is tx-scoped and rebuilt per tx. There is no persistent recognition of `(digest, address)` bindings across transactions; each tx must include the binding VERIFY frame that proves the claim. `MAX_BOUND_SIGNERS = 8` bounds table-population cost and matches approve + swap + repay redemption shapes.
+
+A revoked-secp256k1 account (per EIP-8151, when applicable) with a registered non-secp256k1 signer in `AUTH_MANAGER` resolves only via signer binding; un-bound `ECRECOVER` calls return zero on the miss path because secp256k1 recovery has been zeroed for that address. No silent recovery to a revoked key.
+
+### Validity Window UX
+
+Wallets MUST display `valid_after` / `valid_before` to users before signing. A short `valid_before` window reduces stale-execution risk for swap-like flows; a long window approaches the unbounded behavior. Reverse windows (`valid_after >= valid_before` with both non-zero) are statically invalid and rejected at admission.
